   "title": "gate_arm.sh has become the tree's device-probe gate by accretion, and #497 is the FIRST probe in it on a foreign machine AND CPU family",
   "witness": "harness:gate_arm.sh runs footbridge, PIT and now an SGI/MIPS probe.  The first two at least share this gate's own -E cats machine; the third does not.",
   "note": "*** FILED BECAUSE A COMMENT ALREADY CLAIMED IT WAS.  The #497 gate comment ended 'the right answer is a gate_devices.sh split ... Filed, not done' -- and it was NOT filed: no ledger row, no queue entry, under any phrasing.  Caught by the pass-2 seat while the comment was STAGED. ***  *That is the gap-closes-itself shape: a claim that a process step is complete, shipping in the same commit as the thing it excuses.  A future reader greps for the row, finds nothing, and cannot tell whether the split was considered and rejected or simply forgotten.*  **AND THE PRECEDENT CLAIM WAS ONE STEP SHORT, which the same seat measured.**  I wrote that `gate_arm.sh` already runs footbridge and PIT probes, 'neither an ARM instruction test'.  True -- **but both run `-E cats`, this gate's OWN ARM machine, and the PIT wiring comment says it was placed there BECAUSE 'this is the only gate whose machine it shares'.**  So `#497`'s probe is not the third instance of an existing accretion; it is **the FIRST probe in this gate on a foreign machine AND CPU family**.  My words were true and my implication was generous to my own decision.  **THE FORCING CRITERION, so this row cannot sit forever:** *the NEXT device probe wired into `gate_arm.sh` converts this from FILED to OWED.*  The accretion story guarantees each addition makes the next cheaper, which is exactly how a least-bad accommodation becomes permanent.  **THE OPERATIONAL COST, named rather than left to be discovered:** a red row in `gate_arm` can now mean an SGI/MIPS device regression.  That is an attribution trap for whoever reads the battery output at 3am.  *** OWED AS OF 2026-08-31, BY ITS OWN FORCING CRITERION, AND RAISED low -> med. ***  The #497 gate block filed this row with the criterion written into the gate itself: *\"the NEXT device probe wired into this gate converts it from filed to OWED.\"*  #498's `sgi_de_width_probe.py` is that probe, wired in the same commit that records this.  **A pre-specified trigger that fires and is ignored is worse than one never written, because the next reader trusts it.**  `gate_arm.sh` now runs THREE device detectors that have nothing to do with ARM -- the pit8253 block, #497's sgi_re and #498's sgi_de -- purely because it is the only gate with probe infrastructure and a machine they share.  *The split was not done in this round on purpose: it is a harness round owing its own negative controls, and holding a HIGH device fix hostage to a gate refactor would be the tail wagging the dog.  What was not acceptable was compounding it silently.*",
